From ca30474385f090546b0ccb8910471a001f84b77d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Geonmo Ryu <geonmo@kisti.re.kr>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:51:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] pool: abort the HTTP connection when an HTTP-TPC pull is
 cancelled

Motivation:
The remote-HTTP mover copies the GET response body with
HttpEntity#writeTo.  If the write to the replica fails, e.g. with
ClosedByInterruptException after the mover was cancelled, writeTo
closes the content stream, which reads the rest of the body from the
remote server.  The mover stays CANCELED until the whole file has
arrived and holds an HTTP-TPC connection slot.

Modification:
Copy the body from the entity's content stream.  If the copy fails,
abort the connection (ConnectionReleaseTrigger#abortConnection)
instead of closing the stream.

Result:
A cancelled HTTP-TPC pull ends promptly and releases its connection.

(backport of dCache/dcache#8327 for the GSDC site build)

Fixes: #8301
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Geonmo Ryu <geonmo@kisti.re.kr>
